  {
   "kind": "slider-design-pleasure",
   "id": "anchor_main-points",
   "title": "WHY FIRST 36 ?",
   "intro": "",
   "items": [
    {
     "title": "Joy in Planing Made easy",
     "text": "When the First 36 starts to plane in 14 knots of wind, the joy is not something you plan for. It just happens. And when sailing makes you feel alive, you simply want to sail more."
    },
    {
     "title": "THE DESIGN TEAM",
     "text": "Our designers are not only world-class names from the nautical industry but also passionate sailors and friends. In this project, they found a common goal of designing a true sailing boat for the coming age."
    },
    {
     "title": "MORE THAN JUST 36 FEET",
     "text": "A modern hull design brings about an extensive interior volume. This allows for an interior with the size and comfort of a 40-footer from the previous generation."
    },
    {
     "title": "INDUSTRIALIZED HIGH-TECH",
     "text": "The hull, deck, bulkheads and interior components are fully cored and vacuum infused. Everything contributes to structural strength. To date, this building technique has only been used in racing or expensive niche brands. The result is a very stiff boat, weighing only 4.800 kg."
    },
    {
     "title": "VARIABLE COCKPIT",
     "text": "The cockpit is modular, as it needs to address a wide variety of setups. Removable bench extensions transform the cockpit area into a comfortable cruising lounge.\nWhen extensions are removed, the cockpit has an ergonomic and efficient racing/shorthanded setup."
    }
   ],
